      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew around a railroad stop on the Atlantic Coast Line, which spurred early prosperity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.floridasmart.com/city-guide/polk-city",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1925 Polk City incorporated as a town and later became a city in 2005, marking its evolution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polk_City%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city is named after Polk County, itself named for President James K. Polk, the 11th U.S. president.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polk_City%2C_Florida",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Fantasy of Flight, an aviation museum founded by pilot Kermit Weeks, is the city’s most famous landmark.",
